WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:04.920
Hi, friends!

2
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:07.420
Let's go back in time!

3
00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:11.160
Long, long ago, there were dinosaurs.

4
00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:12.800
Look!

5
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.640
This dinosaur has horns!

6
00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.260
It is a Carnotaurus!

7
00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:22.100
Its name means meat-eating bull.

8
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.940
It lived in Argentina, in South America.

9
00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.520
That was about 70 million years ago.

10
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:32.580
Look at its head!

11
00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:35.380
It had two horns above its eyes.

12
00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:37.640
Just like a big bull!

13
00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:41.580
Maybe it used them to push other Carnotaurus.

14
00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:44.320
Its head was short and tall.

15
00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:47.700
Carnotaurus was big.

16
00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:50.640
It was about as long as a small bus!

17
00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.980
It was as heavy as one or two cars!

18
00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.900
Now look at its long legs!

19
00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:01.100
Scientists think it was a fast runner.

20
00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.180
Its strong tail may have helped it run.

21
00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:06.220
Zoom, zoom!

22
00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:09.600
Now look at its arms.

23
00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:12.040
Its arms were super tiny!

24
00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:16.580
For its size, its arms were tinier than T. rex's!

25
00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:20.120
Its little fingers probably could not move!

26
00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:24.220
This rock shows Carnotaurus skin!

27
00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:28.120
Its skin had lots of small, bumpy scales.

28
00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:32.840
Very few meat-eating dinosaurs left skin prints like this!

29
00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:38.540
Scientists found its bones in Argentina in 1984.

30
00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:42.750
Its real bones are in a museum in Buenos Aires.

31
00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:46.940
Copies of it stand in museums all over the world!

32
00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:50.360
Let's say the words!

33
00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:52.720
Carnotaurus!

34
00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:56.500
Dinosaur!

35
00:01:58.540 --> 00:01:59.690
Head!

36
00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:02.990
Horns!

37
00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:06.290
Big!

38
00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:09.540
Legs!

39
00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:12.910
Fast!

40
00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:16.480
Tail!

41
00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:19.670
Arms!

42
00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:23.150
Tiny!

43
00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.530
Skin!

44
00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:29.720
Bones!

45
00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:33.440
Great job!

46
00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:37.180
Bye-bye, Carnotaurus!

47
00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:38.550
Wait!

48
00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:40.860
Does it say moo?

49
00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:43.080
No!

50
00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:46.540
It is a dinosaur, not a bull!

51
00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:48.700
See you next time!
